{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q209367","formula":"C₅H₅NO₂","hill":"C5H5NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":5.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Methyl cyanoacrylate","uk":"Метилціаноакрилат"},"descriptions":{"en":"Methyl cyanoacrylate (MCA; also sometimes referred to as α-cyanoacrylate or alpha-cyanoacrylate) is an organic compound that contains several functional groups: a methyl ester, a nitrile, and an alkene. It is a colorless liquid with low viscosity. Its chief use is as the main component of cyanoacrylate glues, commonly named superglue.","uk":"Метилціаноакрила́т (МЦА; також іноді α-ціаноакрилат або альфа-ціаноакрилат) — органічна сполука, що містить кілька функціональних груп: метиловий естер, нітрил та алкен. Безбарвна рідина з низькою в'язкістю. Головне застосування — основний компонент ціаноакрилатних клеїв."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":8711,"mass":111.1,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC(=O)C(=C)C#N","inchikey":"MWCLLHOVUTZFKS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methyl 2-cyanoprop-2-enoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"8711","atoms":13,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.07,"y":0.919,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.563,"y":-1.331,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":2.328,"y":1.448,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.761,"y":-0.408,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":0.719,"y":-0.575,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.467,"y":1.23,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.206,"y":-1.823,"z":0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":1.607,"y":0.54,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.945,"y":0.83,"z":-0.899,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.573,"y":2.318,"z":0.001,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.943,"y":0.83,"z":0.902,"el":"H"},{"x":0.565,"y":-2.699,"z":0.002,"el":"H"},{"x":2.277,"y":-2.011,"z":0.003,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[0,5,1],[1,3,2],[2,7,3],[3,4,1],[4,6,2],[4,7,1],[5,8,1],[5,9,1],[5,10,1],[6,11,1],[6,12,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name"